// TAB technique letters on a notation staff and on a tab staff: @tap (T),
// @hammeron (H), @pulloff (P) and @pluck's finger letter. THE FIRST BOOK IN THE
// TREE THAT DRAWS ANY OF THEM — on 2026-08-28 not one of the 572 tracked .lys
// wrote one, which is why a letter drawn 0.383 ss INTO its notehead survived
// (reported that day). The low notes are the point: they take the letter BELOW,
// which is the side where the ink grows toward the head.
// See TabTechniqueLetterTests for the identity these letters are held to.
octave absolute
title "TAB technique letters"
time 4/4
part gtr { clef treble }
section S {
  gtr {
    c4@tap e@tap g@tap b@hammeron |
    c'4@tap e'@pulloff g'@tap b'@hammeron |
    e4@pluck(p) a@pluck(i) b@pluck(m) e'@pluck(a) |
  }
}
form main { ~S }
score main "tab-technique-letters" {
  staff gtr
  tab gtr
}
